ct} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308324}] :question/id #uuid "5ea8ee90-f780-5300-8262-a562939b4083" :question/math-academy-id "q-333141" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[2,\\text{ }-1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,\\text{ }0]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}\\cdot {{field-1}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\cdot {{field-2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-3}}\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{4t}\\to $ \n{{field-4}}\nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach \n{{field-5}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/1d/1d2a232b4351c84871d89ba25384aa53777760355ceea6458b07fba9c0a9ed78.png)\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line.\n\nSince ${e}^{3t}\\to $ \n{{field-7}}\nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach \n{{field-8}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/12/122759a459c8dd56dbe69c44c0da4ccffbbc660465fbedc7457e17b42430436e.png)\n\nFinally, since the dominant eigenvalue is \n{{field-9}},\n solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector \n{{field-10}} \nas they move away from the origin.\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/fa/fa5033f974e501bb8bf6960753b1706569f5ed59c3dec6d22e8b200317f2a487.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{4t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/1d/1d2a232b4351c84871d89ba25384aa53777760355ceea6458b07fba9c0a9ed78.png)\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=0\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line.\n\nSince ${e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/12/122759a459c8dd56dbe69c44c0da4ccffbbc660465fbedc7457e17b42430436e.png)\n\nFor this particular system, we have\n\n$$\n0<{\\lambda }_{2}<{\\lambda }_{1}\n$$\n\nthus, ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ is the dominant eigenvalue.\n\nSince the dominant eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}=4,$  solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector  ${v}_{1}$ as they move away from the origin.\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/fc/fcaa3ba63a1e6ad061eecf1f72caf3c9f8ba78b014eff044ee5be682e1325128.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "883c0be6-db2c-578b-a765-bcd926761786" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306454} {:answer/id #uuid "af991b60-a7f8-59eb-ab14-0e73cf86c317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306805} :answer-field/id #uuid "13ff12f4-89dd-5fa0-9425-9bd2395274a2" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b4a1d8a-78de-5585-b9ff-0da35a92dd17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305566} {:answer/id #uuid "3241e779-8378-5379-a985-2c9e9e29c622" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305623} {:answer/id #uuid "4bdb855f-49c1-5dbb-8457-e473f2807aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305877} {:answer/id #uuid "de8e91c4-fe47-50c2-a14b-26f68c3f7ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307216} {:answer/id #uuid "ef63445d-97f5-5cef-9324-14a470e9c272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305566} :answer-field/id #uuid "14c0f26d-f89c-50b9-996e-693f154c6ce0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307587} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c266a3-ab72-5fdb-84a3-7ce02abceaff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305678} {:an