1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{ }3]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-2}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach \n{{field-3}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-6}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach \n{{field-7}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-8}}." :question/worked-solution "The straight-line solutions of the system have the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-3x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/ed/ed058963b391a4cdc66b2ab48483906a4d07759681c1f24e47ffc9e10775895f.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}<0.$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/6c/6c92028370c86431ddc6ccd9513c273054d98b5add159e1bddf5a2e11751d987.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{away from the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308361 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "178d8399-2cdd-5266-ba88-b0eee07ffd44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305368} {:answer/id #uuid "34a5083f-61a1-5255-9ef8-455ca853d7dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305654} {:answer/id #uuid "60038b1a-036a-532b-9bfb-108211f32ab9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306077} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8d663d-65f9-5e20-afc6-5748e9149353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305654} :answer-field/id #uuid "07999d18-28a6-58bc-a63e-359d96ea1ccc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44c3f488-6a55-5566-ad3b-d57fb079156c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305826} {:answer/id #uuid "d7ec69ff-7a6d-553e-b383-8e5a53990638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307153} {:answer/id #uuid "e8cd87f4-38e4-5161-a84c-452856df6d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 1759