eld-7" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044a0690-55ba-5c10-a9ce-6daf70b82583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422018} {:answer/id #uuid "36069637-bc2f-5c4e-8eb6-254856b3234e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422040} {:answer/id #uuid "79933aee-d57f-550e-94b4-aef9a4d6f268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422018} :answer-field/id #uuid "e96b3b83-4377-53a0-8ef9-b0ddb316497b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422151}] :question/id #uuid "a8dac9e3-6d64-5716-8812-6c8cce0790e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-333600" :question/problem "![](images/45/450d43a4cbf6dad8d54edbb66fc4a6e44e491290e1dc5d1303057fb0eb7928a7.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two real, distinct eigenvalues is shown above.\nThe eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }2]^{T},$ respectively. \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-2}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach \n{{field-3}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-6}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach \n{{field-7}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-8}}.\n\nFinally, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector {{field-9}} as they move away from the origin, the dominant eigenvalue is \n{{field-10}}.\n\nTherefore,\n{{field-11}} \n$>0.$" :question/worked-solution "The straight-line solutions of the system have the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/2d/2dace7c4f02fa0575d70264f33805d15470fa0894622c4d26d80fc1221aa2c54.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{away from the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}>0.$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-2x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/40/40f0bf749448807b1a3aa2b593ae2e30acf26fabedbdc45da75e338e84c328f2.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{away from the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}>0.$\n\nSo, for this particular system, both eigenvalues are positive. The dominant eigenvalue is the one with the greatest magnitude.\n\nNow, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector ${v}_{2}$ as they move away from the origin, the dominant eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, ${\\lambda }_{2}>{\\lambda }_{1}>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c3bb420-a062-589d-8a15-df82a283ae00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445839} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ac8000-0724-5a0d-830b-1dc063abd8bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445839} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e68026c-5b3a-5dec-9a24-e484784bb566" :answer-field/key "field-10" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62bae53b-ff93-5d73-a244-bee46f728e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445840} {:answer/id #uuid "86244ec8-b8e9-5ffa-a880-ffe1b9fb6f4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445847} {:answer/id #uuid "e1608a5c-6093-5262-8851-7c467dc237cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445856} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc8bc61-7a28-516e-aa2b-b1428cea56d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445840} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c0f095b-980a-5fcb-926f-7d81b562d855" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82469ff2-6605-5dc2-9350