pe {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a3e4a1c-c6ba-518c-a073-ef3580a687e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445842} {:answer/id #uuid "b4f91994-a0ed-50cc-8db4-764ca1da532e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445849} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2d0de9b-f4b3-5990-bc03-9e94612c7ac1" :answer-field/key "field-9" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445871}] :question/id #uuid "0b89fafc-c196-5520-9710-898a3b3a16af" :question/math-academy-id "q-333488" :question/problem "![](images/a2/a21b978aaab9569ae4dcae346116e51b5248fdf8f3cff461411a2140f70a6a4c.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two real, distinct eigenvalues is shown above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[2,1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-2}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach \n{{field-3}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-6}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach \n{{field-7}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-8}}.\n\nFinally, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector {{field-9}} as they move towards the origin, the eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior (dominant eigenvalue) is \n{{field-10}}.\n\nTherefore,\n{{field-11}} \n$<0.$" :question/worked-solution "The straight-line solutions of the system have the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/ab/abdb72ad4cd1bbde4e53c901b6b285904078f456a3fa52ab667bf1675d2d68dd.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}<0.$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=-x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/cf/cf3cb4b5756e5f382cd798d371e3d3e797f5ba0a146cdb8424ed1c62c051564b.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nSo, for this particular system, both eigenvalues are negative. The eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior (dominant eigenvalue) is the one closest to $0.$\n\nNow, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector ${v}_{1}$ as they move towards the origin, the eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior is ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\n\nTherefore, ${\\lambda }_{2}<{\\lambda }_{1}<0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ba0ee72-f98e-5452-b0ab-851fc7dee945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529635} {:answer/id #uuid "64868afb-1001-5a9d-99c2-2b2230a9edbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529828} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb01b62-5037-5dd9-a766-4716610f0f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529828} :answer-field/id #uuid "05e61a3b-bbaf-5bab-b901-9321031c732c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530219} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47a4601c-9108-57e2-9ba0-39e7fea9913b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529748} {:answer/id #uuid "521cc0d6-9128-5cdb-8865-fa00b45f6b36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529776} {:answer/id #uuid "af5ae64a-6665-5281-a276-9023eb63b26d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530018} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b91c76-5c7e-5fc7-813a-a33ad8c8a4db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530018} :answer-field/id #uuid "070804c8-3b5d-555e-994a-50be2a1aa3e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530222} {:answer-field/choices [{:ans