answer/id #uuid "ca69a69f-21c8-5b82-b9c2-4749e4f73579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529773} :answer-field/id #uuid "c57c0f33-d9b1-5dc9-8b98-ee2e345de9ec" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c71fdc-ed83-5969-8583-60828a4fa22f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529589} {:answer/id #uuid "64bac435-ca66-5d14-9536-e149843494ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529831} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5801f6a-9756-5a5a-8061-21b3d880aef0" :answer-field/key "field-9" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2503c449-3232-57ca-959d-3ad79d4daa64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529660} {:answer/id #uuid "a0800f5e-7a43-5446-a6f2-efcb6f34f91d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529660} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ce54c2-58ca-563f-a943-2b87144d054f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530366} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0130011a-855a-504c-8ed9-de640a85cf65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529577} {:answer/id #uuid "53308e85-0ea9-5376-ba91-1d38df29c1c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529778} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb0e05e-e814-59a0-b300-e445fc5ab637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529577} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddb27815-0b88-5fe1-9bd9-3f33b06ca48a" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530382}] :question/id #uuid "22670f3b-ee2e-505b-bc5c-db0616554dee" :question/math-academy-id "q-333345" :question/problem "![](images/51/51ffadb1da41e6a1fe06fdc9c14a6967d3a80b4d26c6a830a401105e0f18bbf5.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two real, distinct eigenvalues is shown above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,2]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,2]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-2}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-3}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-6}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-7}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-8}}.\n\nFinally, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector {{field-9}} as they move towards the origin, the eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior (dominant eigenvalue) is \n{{field-10}}.\n\nTherefore,\n{{field-11}} \n$<0.$" :question/worked-solution "The straight-line solutions of the system have the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=-2x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/6e/6ea2d64a390187a28cfcd1c2692e97e5dc2ca5cb37649ba12cf71864e36958ea.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}<0.$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=2x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f2340cbff80765a5d3b551e87eb4207eebad05970e366ceeccd7bb142c0b677.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nSo, for this particular system, both eigenvalues are negative. The eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior (dominant eigenvalue) is the one closest to $0.$\n\nNow, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector ${v}_{1}$ as they move towards the origin, the eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior is ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\n\nTherefore, ${\\lambda }_{2}<{\\lambda }_{1}<0.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parameters of a System Given Its Phase Portrait"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166918 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166543 :question/id #uuid "1c7567cf-f861-5088-b43e-ff94fcff0c91" :question/math-academy-id "e-21634" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=9x(t)+6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-6x(t)-6y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_1=6$ and $\\lambda_2=-3,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are $\\mathbf{v}_1 = [-2, \\ 1]^T$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2 = [-1, \\ 2]^T,$ respectively. Complete the following statements about the system by filling in the blanks.\n\nIdentify stable and unstable lines, and classify the equilibrium point (origin)." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n![](images/9b/9b19dee8e197c29ab1802c7ea500f07185f24885702027a9726de39a91eacd9e.svg)\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ![](images/15/150fe59c158191129d89c43a1bb569e5c88b686c4365a6b06e661343f85b5e7d.svg) has the equation \n\n$$\ny= -\\dfrac12x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n![](images/f6/f6679165a59f48eb2944f4f8337ba990f2e82619e5e2a03308e0b4f663f9137c.svg)\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t \\to \\infty.$ So, $y=-\\dfrac12x$ is an unstable line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ![](images/e1/e1dcfabda7582534138b11b45a14cd8a8a9923c02d743ff99af08e487bcda254.svg) has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-2x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n![](images/3b/3ba48e81a2f6239f7cf0389017d823b87d558ded003eb6470ff6dc9078808b87.svg)\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t \\to \\infty.$ So, $y=-2x$ is a stable line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is a saddle point. \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/27/2710e11309547500aa3e9ba89f31281cbbc28244509046ed25a6c151c10c23ed.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35492718-d2d7-5c9d-9c02-1ef6ae0445d0" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167213 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ebd8b78-6d37-5c4b-a5c9-4b102c04ca8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164313} {:answer/id #uuid "08d004a0-b250-5576-be4c-61b2647bbecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164314} {:answer/id #uuid "78e61936-0ca1-5efe-90e4-c8d63f8681f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164315} {:answer/id #uuid "7e91305d-8c0f-518f-9857-e7f7107cab52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164316}] :answer-field/id #uuid "63dbe9f5-e7eb-5e10-8990-0bb5bfba9e13" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164312} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "907a6164-e1b6-5986-9dca-115cd1a65f63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164318} {:answer/id #uuid "5efb952c-f79f-559c-9639-7cbba5d634b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164319}] :answer-field/id #uuid "139d243c-34ef-5981-9b57-3a2a9b4e59ec" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3ea8aa5-b8f2-58d5-8495-c00a312eee23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164321} {:answer/id #uuid "a80cc57c-3023-51d6-a518-30fbe50cccbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164322}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f72b5cac-09dc-59da-b9e1-5feb4d889cae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type