stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391251} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef32066-7efb-5518-b08e-5b73f307a698" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391250} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c1d23b5-f76a-5cfb-b2b7-024a619b5bc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable node (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391254} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ef6ad1-d41a-592f-9f2a-dafc9e0ed0c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391255} {:answer/id #uuid "29fe338f-9f99-59e0-b948-9af05832bed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable node (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable node (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391254} :answer-field/id #uuid "244f6b3b-3578-574d-94fd-0dcddcc4492b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391253}] :question/id #uuid "f735f61a-0791-5bf2-b5e1-a997e0f18859" :question/math-academy-id "q-333646" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-3x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[2,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n$y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{-4t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-4t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable node (sink)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/63/6337a670b6fa73c4c21759b600269cb83d808a1c13026c90e2d02519fa31cd67.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308481 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5edddb8d-f8be-588f-bd8b-edcd12fbaf71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306065} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c4960d-a6f2-56aa-ac63-26b326dbeeb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307019} {:answer/id #uuid "c973fd6a-c086-5d79-be1f-0a6dd1ad4fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307019} :answer-field/id #uuid "088e3f3a-55da-51fc-ae61-71abf333f08f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307551} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c0c6c6-859b-5201-853f-a06bd6868bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305493} {:answer/id #uuid "62b35c1d-607a-5303-be36-d86e52577629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306107} {:answer/id #uuid "9e922f86-0c6b-54ee-bb1a-730dab48b448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306107} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e1a049f-07a7-5535-8353-1dc98ba2619e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b7bb785-d8f8-5514-97ce-91c00d71b394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305250} {:answer/id #uuid "42ff7225-7f43-5acd-aa62-38d9e84dc31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305812} {:answer/id #uuid "a55dbfe8-4f29-590e-9001-a28c8bcadc55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306707} {:answer/id #uuid "f130d46b-06cb-5394-91fd-d6c98a253116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305250} :answer-field/id #uuid "b421be58-2656-5af8-8c40-40c306a90752" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308091} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17725bd1-749d-522a-a04d-5e14bb6dae0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305367} {:answer/id #uuid "4c682b61-48dd-5173-b98e-7d98e0a3df68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable node (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305888} {:answer/id #uuid "990ecfe5-7b15-5b2f-8621-7277b78f435b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306581} {:answer/id #uuid "f190138d-4418-5067-901f-9ddbf88ea8aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable node (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305367} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed482f9e-1956-5576-a6d5-59c3c2d5265d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308266}] :question/id #uuid "ca7ddbc3-cff0-528a-94e0-d6fbf22a4ad5" :question/math-academy-id "q-333637" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=x(t)+3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n{{field-1}} is {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n$y=-x$ is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a saddle point}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/a0/a09d50fa36b2748fb1c65ed16e20d950afbbabc18884ff8718cf1571c4e13b0e.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308483 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01495a53-7dfd-544b-a887-b616e881178d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305163} {:answer/id #uuid "450b6c82-095a-59e2-a36b-91516732dfc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305830} {:answer/id #uuid "dde3aa96-b118-5380-8664-eb9c127a7dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307208} {:answer/id #uuid "f3aa0e46-5b18-5300-b699-39279f33ae31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305163} :answer-field/id #uuid "05101cad-9c0f-59eb-a3bd-092249b94171" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5107d61c-9632-5d00-8097-f4094a5c7519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "an unstable node (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305938} {:answer/id #uuid "bd19d70c-61ff-5810-86e9-5bd0ed6440f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable node (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306917} {:answer/id #uuid "d7467d4c-2543-584e-8f87-66c20d15092c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable node (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 175921863071