{c}_{2}{e}^{-6t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-3t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-6t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable node (sink)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/a2/a21b978aaab9569ae4dcae346116e51b5248fdf8f3cff461411a2140f70a6a4c.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3550c5b-1a8d-5dcc-94d9-d43ecbc42265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391228} {:answer/id #uuid "df63b9f7-a38a-5edb-993f-36ceedd86317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391229} :answer-field/id #uuid "c76521b0-e06a-5475-a7d5-6e2974a8f112" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391227} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5312169-7d7a-54df-9140-8a7bb5968066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391231} {:answer/id #uuid "950b0d68-2c7b-597b-b535-d524113f3c61" :answe