241} :answer-field/id #uuid "e05694af-fcc2-57e8-a41a-79ef3c0578f2" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391238}] :question/id #uuid "d111108f-9aed-5eb7-8811-2065601ee640" :question/math-academy-id "q-333640" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=x(t)+4y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-2,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[0,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n$y=-\\frac{1}{2}x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\nx=0.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $x=0$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/0d/0d9e032bfffa68f487347d6c169999e313247e89ef7de3fae28edb216dcf718f.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422155 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c7c5dd4-985b-5405-bb39-51253042d52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422021} {:answer/id #uuid "7e7acc82-e6c4-5dec-befb-675ccec0903d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422072} {:answer/id #uuid "919301d7-68f2-5782-915a-8f4d378d4451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422084} {:answer/id #uuid "cffa05d2-1031-5c3b-942d-069e218dd818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422105} :answer-field/id #uuid "17f61bfc-2b2f-5780-a0d3-c92c029fb198" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14bc55e1-31d7-5798-9f51-9e810ae5b145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422027} {:answer/id #uuid "b39d43c4-a1f9-54c2-8f94-0bfd592ebd10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422093} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b80139d-bc1e-5645-8de4-30d2db8afdf1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a24f1ef-649e-5645-995e-2f802b1f4380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422061} {:answer/id #uuid "c09b78a5-7042-5294-99d6-32a590ecb504" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422061} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ad00cd6-77d9-5b4b-9995-246f45c8c4b3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422132} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116aa627-74f3-55db-9c3e-276499470af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable node (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422023} {:answer/id #uuid "2e978d2d-0d3b-58eb-a366-69213e6f3246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422034} {:answer/id #uuid "88101903-0398-5bd1-af51-4e947d7e70ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable node (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422034} :answer-field/id #uuid "80de76c1-383f-57a7-b028-3b3844fe8b00" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422144}] :question/id #uuid "5c8c49ce-183e-525d-b069-5b56d43e69f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-333625" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }3]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}} is {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n$y=-3x$ is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-3x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-3x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a saddle point}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/f2/f20c6478af528b45ab2ea7dfded3e835c49a79178e11d7dd06bb13760874bbdb.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530434 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09127fa6-751e-5de5-9626-f7c3ade21701" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529594} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbd7798-2750-5c2f-b9ba-11c058833061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529594} :answer-field/id #uuid "52e5d219-347a-59f7-9240-fa2c72d0c7a8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530279} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0adbae6f-09ad-5e85-adc2-3211170c6c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529597} 